<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese four-month car sales fall 3.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese four-month car sales fall 3.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto-Dealers Association (ACAP) announced the following new cars registrations:</p>
<p>    April	1997 18,919 vs 19,117 (down 1.0 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/April  1997 74,561 vs 77,099 (down 3.3 pct)</p>
<p>First four months by manufacturers' markets share (percentage in brackets). Comparative figures refer to same period 1996):</p>
<p>    Fiat	10,692 (14.34) vs 11,510 (14.93)</p>
<p>    Opel	10,218 (13.70) vs 10,763 (13,96)</p>
<p>    Renault    9,770 (13.10) vs 10,894 (14.13)</p>
<p>    Ford	 7,927 (10,63) vs  7,947 (10.31)</p>
<p>    Volkswagen 6,491 ( 8,71) vs  6,128 ( 7.95)</p>
<p>    Citroen    5,144 ( 6,90) vs  3,898 ( 5.06)</p>
<p>    Peugeot    4,219 ( 5,66) vs  5,120 ( 6.64)</p>
<p>    Honda	2,587 ( 3,47) vs  2,818 ( 3.66)</p>
<p>    Seat	 2,255 ( 3,02) vs  2,537 ( 3.29)</p>
<p>    Rover	1,732 ( 2,32) vs  2,918 ( 3.78)</p>
</text>
